{%- comment -%}
  Cool colourway for the Cooling Collection.

  Same type, same layout, same components — only the palette moves, from the
  warm heritage ground to a cold one. It reads as the same shop, filed under a
  different season.

  Written at .pl.pl.pl rather than .pl.pl on purpose. Every pl-* section renders
  its own <link> to pl-styles.css, so a section further down the page would
  otherwise reload the sheet after this block and win on source order. One extra
  class beats that outright.

  Contrast, measured against the ground each colour actually lands on:
    ink   #0F1C22 on bone  16.4:1     bone on clay        5.3:1
    ink-2 #2C3E47 on bone  10.5:1     bone on clay-dk     7.3:1
    ink-3 #546770 on oat    5.1:1     bone on moss       13.2:1
    clay-text on bone       6.2:1     on-dark-lede on moss 10.4:1
    clay-text on oat        5.7:1     on-dark-body on moss  7.5:1
    clay-onDark on moss     4.9:1
    moss-3 on moss          6.4:1

  Usage:
    {% render 'pl-cool-palette' %}                    always apply
    {% render 'pl-cool-palette', product: product %}  apply only if it's a
                                                      cooling product
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign apply = true
  if product != blank
    assign hay = product.tags | join: ',' | append: ',' | append: product.type | downcase
    assign apply = false
    if hay contains 'cooling' or hay contains 'elevated'
      assign apply = true
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if apply -%}
<style>
  .pl.pl.pl {
    --ink:        #0F1C22;
    --ink-2:      #2C3E47;
    --ink-3:      #546770;
    --bone:       #F6F9FA;
    --oat:        #E6EFF2;
    --sand:       #C7DAE1;
    --moss:       #12303A;
    --moss-2:     #1D424E;
    --moss-3:     #8FB6C4;
    --clay:       #16708A;
    --clay-dk:    #0F5A70;
    --clay-text:  #12657D;
    --clay-tint:  #DCEEF3;
    --gold:       #12657D;
    --focus:      #16708A;
    --clay-onDark: #4FA3BE;
    --on-dark-lede: #CFE2E9;
    --on-dark-body: #A6C3CE;
    --on-dark-rgb:  214, 233, 240;
  }
</style>
{%- endif -%}
